# XCU sact
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# SCCS files are made and inspected only with the SCCS utilities (admin,
# get, delta, prs and friends); the file format is unspecified so nothing
# reads the files directly. A missing companion utility makes the test
# UNRESOLVED. Login names, dates and the diagnostic texts are never compared
# literally.

assertion  XCU.sact.001
anchor     utilities/sact.html#STDOUT
anchor     utilities/sact.html#DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       After get -e, sact writes a line with the SID read, the new SID,
           a login, a date and a time.
test       t/001-pending-line.sh

assertion  XCU.sact.002
anchor     utilities/sact.html#STDOUT
anchor     utilities/sact.html#STDERR
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       With no pending edit, and after delta completes an edit, nothing
           is written to standard output.
test       t/002-nothing-pending.sh

assertion  XCU.sact.003
anchor     utilities/sact.html#STDOUT
anchor     utilities/sact.html#OPERANDS
anchor     utilities/sact.html#STDIN
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       With several files each name is written as a heading before its
           lines.
test       t/003-several-files.sh
